    },
    "message": "Write the history index with a write-ahead log\n\nReaders waited for a long index write (a fork copying its parent's rows)\nfor five to six seconds. The index now uses SQLite's WAL journal mode, so\nreaders read the last commit while a write is in progress; synchronous\nstays FULL. After each commit the log returns to the index file and is\nemptied, and it is bounded to 16 MiB after automatic returns. Readers\nopen SQLite's -shm and -wal files beside the index, which the frame cache\ntest no longer counts as saved files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
